## Hardwired Cross-Discipline Contracts

1. Recording secrets, tokens, or credentials into memory is unconditionally prohibited. If rule or skill secret-hygiene is adopted, execution adheres to rules/secret-hygiene.md for credential scanning and incident remediation.
2. If rule or skill guard-secret-paths is adopted, execution adheres to rules/guard-secret-paths.md to prevent database operations targeting guarded paths.
3. If rule or skill plain-writing is adopted, execution adheres to rules/plain-writing.md for fact phrasing and entity summaries.
4. If rule or skill audit-harness is adopted, execution adheres to rules/audit-harness.md to persist confirmed architectural decisions and invariants.
